Notice for data/brain_landmarks.npz
(written by scripts/fetch_datasets.py --brain on 2026-10-22T21:01:22Z)

The file holds the `schizophrenia.dat` array of the package (Bookstein's schizophrenia
data: 13 near-midsagittal brain landmarks from MR images of 28 subjects, data kindly
provided by Fred Bookstein; source: Bookstein, F. L. (1996) Biometrics, biomathematics
and the morphometric synthesis, Bulletin of Mathematical Biology 58:313-365).  R's
13 x 2 x 28 array was rearranged to points (28, 13, 2) float64 in the package's
subject and landmark order, with labels 0 = control (subjects 1-14) and
1 = schizophrenia (subjects 15-28) as the package documents.  Values are unchanged.

The arrays were extracted from the source tarball of the R package "shapes"
version 1.2.8 by Ian L. Dryden (https://cran.r-project.org/package=shapes,
https://github.com/iandryden/shapes), which is distributed under the GNU
General Public License version 2 (GPL-2).  They are redistributed here under
the same licence, GPL-2, with this notice.  The full licence text is in
LICENSES/GPL-2.txt and at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt.
The GPL-2 applies to this data file; the rest of this repository is MIT-licensed
(see LICENSE).

Source tarball: shapes_1.2.8.tar.gz
